--- OUTCOME SUMMARY ---
The single-shot full-RTL co-synthesis of all four real HLS IPs + scheduler
hit THREE successive Vitis/Vivado tool failures (detailed below). The
deliverable is therefore an HONEST INTEGRATION PROJECTION built from the
five components' real, independently-measured synthesis results — NOT a
single co-synth report. A true single-netlist integration needs the proper
Vitis-HLS export_design → Vivado IP-integrator flow (a multi-hour v1 task).

--- the three synth attempts ---
v1 (multithreaded): Vivado helper process failed to read its own internal
    file scripts/rt/data/lib_core.tcl. (File exists — intermittent helper
    spawn race on this host.)
v2 (single-threaded, set_param general.maxThreads 1): got past the helper
    issue, then ERROR [Synth 8-439] — module '<top>_sdiv_..._ip' not found.
    Root cause: the HLS softmax NORM loop infers a signed divide, which Vitis
    HLS implements via a Xilinx Divider LogiCORE. That core is delivered as an
    XCI/IP-generated netlist, NOT plain Verilog — so the raw HLS RTL is missing
    the three '<top>_sdiv_..._ip' modules.
v3 (+ behavioral divider stubs): all 3 missing _ip modules supplied as
    port-compatible behavioral dividers (coord/reports/T0031/divider_ip_stubs.v).
    Synthesis got through RTL elaboration + Part Resource Summary, then Vivado
    CRASHED: "Abnormal program termination (EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT)", rc 0x80000003.
    No usable stack trace in hs_err_pidNNNN.log. Most likely cause: the
    integration leaves thousands of ap_memory ports (xmod_attn's Q/K/V = 64
    banks each, vit_encoder's 12×4 weight arrays × 8 banks, ...) dangling at the
    mr_vla_full_top boundary; that volume of unconnected ports appears to
    overrun a Vivado internal limit / memory on this 16 GB host.

--- WHY single-shot raw-RTL integration is the wrong approach (lesson) ---
HLS-generated RTL is NOT meant to be hand-instantiated into a parent netlist.
The supported path is: Vitis HLS `export_design` → packaged IP (IP-XACT) →
Vivado IP integrator / block design, where each IP's ap_memory / ap_ctrl
interfaces are connected through adapters and the tool manages the divider
LogiCORE generation. That flow is a multi-hour engineering task and is the
correct v1 for T0031.

